---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/hub.css';
---
<Base title='Privacy' description='What this site processes, why, and your rights, in plain language.'>
<div class="topbar"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="brand"><span class="dot"></span> San Juan Riparian Watch</div>
  <a class="back" href="/">← back to the story</a>
</div></div>

<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow">// privacy</div>
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="lede">A plain-language account of what this site processes and why. It's a personal portfolio
    project, not a commercial service, and it's built to collect as little as possible.</p>
</div></header>

<div class="wrap">

<section>
  <h2>Reading the pages</h2>
  <p>Just browsing the site sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, runs <strong>no analytics or trackers</strong>,
    and loads <strong>no third-party fonts or scripts that would expose your IP</strong>; the fonts are
    served from this domain. Standard web-server access logs (including IP address) may be kept briefly for
    security and abuse prevention, on the basis of legitimate interest.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Using the chat agent</h2>
  <p>If you ask the agent a question, that request is processed to answer it:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose &amp; handling</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Your question</td><td>Sent to the retrieval pipeline and to a large-language-model provider to generate a grounded answer. Please don't enter personal or sensitive information; it isn't needed to ask about the science.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Model provider</td><td>Generation runs on a third-party, OpenAI-compatible LLM API via <strong>OpenRouter</strong> (the model is selectable, e.g. Qwen, Llama, or Ai2's OLMo), which may process the request <strong>outside the EU</strong>. Responses are scrubbed for personal identifiers before they're returned.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>IP address</td><td>Used transiently for per-IP rate-limiting and abuse prevention (legitimate interest). Not used to profile or track you across sites.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Session id</td><td>A random identifier generated fresh on each page load, held in memory to thread a single conversation. It is not a persistent cookie and does not identify you.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note"><span class="t">Retention</span>
    Operational logs and traces are kept only as long as needed for security and debugging, then discarded.
    There is no marketing, no advertising, and no sale or sharing of data for those purposes.</div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag"><b>OpenRouter</b> · LLM generation (model-agnostic)</span>
    <span class="tag"><b>Esri</b> · satellite basemap tiles</span>
    <span class="tag"><b>Hetzner</b> (EU) · hosting</span>
  </div>
  <p>Map tiles are requested from Esri's imagery service when you view a map; your browser contacts them
    directly, as it would for any embedded map.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you can request access to, correction of, or erasure of any personal data held about you,
    and you may object to processing or lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. Because the site keeps
    essentially no identifying records, there is usually nothing to retrieve. But if you have a question or a
    request, contact <a href="mailto:joshua.dell@outlook.com">joshua.dell@outlook.com</a>.</p>
</section>

</div>

